  "problem": "Given that $\u20167u+v\u2016=32$ and $\u2016v\u2016=4$, find the smallest possible value of $\u2016u\u2016.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u20167u+v\u2016 & \\le \u20167u\u2016+\u2016v\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u20167u+v\u2016 & \\le 7\u2016u\u2016+\u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 32 & \\le 7\u2016u\u2016+4 \\\\ 28 & \\le 7\u2016u\u2016 \\\\ 4 & \\le \u2016u\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $\u2016u\u2016$ is $4.$",
